# --- Project documents kept local ---
# CLAUDE.md IS tracked: it states the constraints the project is built against,
# so it ships with the code. These two stay local -- the brief is not ours to
# publish, and IMPLEMENT.md is superseded on ordering by v1plan.md.
ASSIGNMENT.md
IMPLEMENT.md

# --- Panorama runtime state ---
# Cloned sibling repos, per-run artifacts and raw model output. Owner-only on
# disk and never committed: it can contain private repository source.
.panorama/

# --- Python build & cache artifacts ---
# Regenerated from pyproject.toml + uv.lock, so never needed to reproduce.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Virtualenv ---
# ~47MB, machine- and platform-specific. `uv sync` recreates it exactly from
# uv.lock, which IS committed.
.venv/
venv/

# --- Tool caches ---
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
